     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p40-models",
     "replacement": "An **exponential model** uses an exponential equation to describe a real situation.\n\nExamples of exponential models include population growth, compound interest, declining-balance depreciation and radioactive decay.\n\n**Exponential growth**\n\n$y=a(1+r)^x$, where $r>0$ and $x$ is the number of periods\nInitial value\n% increase\nper period as\na decimal\t**Exponential decay**\n\n$y=a(1-r)^x$, where $0<r<1$ and $x$ is the number of periods\nInitial value\n% decrease\nper period as\na decimal",
